  "domain": "ai",
  "definition": "Neural Machine Translation (NMT) is an approach to automated language translation in which end-to-end neural networks \u2014 typically based on encoder-decoder architectures with attention mechanisms \u2014 learn to map source-language sequences directly to target-language sequences from parallel corpora. Unlike earlier statistical phrase-based methods, NMT systems capture long-range dependencies and global sentence context, producing more fluent and contextually accurate translations. The Transformer architecture has become the dominant NMT paradigm since its introduction in 2017.",
